FNFC-01.3 latency probe v3, rebased on FNFC-01.11 (size-only tx buffer reset; same stamps). Temporary, NOT for commit.
Adds stamps inside the fixed "handler" window (RxEnd -> nfc_listener_tx) to localise the ~263 us (step 4).
Apply on top of FNFC-01.3 (instead of v2, not in addition):
  git apply nfc_dumps/pm3_parity/out/2026-10-11-fnfc013/latency_probe_v3.patch
  ./fbt DEBUG=0 --extra-define=NFC_LISTENER_TX_LATENCY_PROBE --extra-define=NFC_LISTENER_TX_LATENCY_PROBE_V3 FLIP_PORT=... flash_usb_full
Output (CLI `log info`): the v2 [PROBE] line, plus one [PROBE3] line per listener TX, DWT cycles @64 MHz relative to RxEnd:
  rx       = after furi_hal_nfc_listener_rx (parser data copy)                       [nfc.c]
  copy     = after bit_buffer_copy_bits into the event buffer                         [nfc.c]
  run      = iso15693_3_listener_run entry (nfc_listener dispatch)                    [iso15693_3_listener.c]
  crc      = after iso13239_crc_check + trim of the request                          [iso15693_3_listener.c]
  handler  = right before the command handler (flags/addressing/UID checks done)     [iso15693_3_listener_i.c]
  send     = iso15693_3_listener_send_frame entry (handler + extension done)          [iso15693_3_listener_i.c]
  crc_app  = after the response CRC append                                           [iso15693_3_listener_i.c]
  tx_enter = nfc_listener_tx entry (same as v2)
Remove with: git apply -R .../latency_probe_v3.patch

